      "message": "Ah yes, my comment was actually building on top of the old patch(3). I was suggesting to pass `iova` and `size` to domain_unmap and let it figure out size expansion and all (as was assumed in patch 3 that the host does size expansion correctly so why not pkvm do it?). And make domain_unmap return size so host know what was actually unmapped.\n\nBut I see, for unmapping an arbitrary range [a, b], where [a, c] is a partial superpage from the top, (c, d) is good unmap range, and [d, b] is again a partial superpage from the bottom, making sure [a, c] and [d, b] don\u0027t exist is still tricky and complex. So I guess, we can drop this idea.",
